{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WHY THE LIVE CLOUD BRIDGE IS NOT HIT: the trigger is an issue MOVING BETWEEN PROJECTS, and this\nproject's Jira tickets are not moved. That is untriggered conditions, not immunity — the binding is\nkeyed on a mutable identifier on Cloud exactly as it is on DC.\n\nRetiring my earlier 'pre-existing, not DC-specific, therefore follow-up' framing. It was true and\nself-serving. Self-hosted DC admins move projects routinely, so DC raises the probability of the\ntrigger while the defect itself is shared."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785509609844902001,"uuid":"82e8265b-4a09-4409-aa22-31e6b3023e61"}